{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollisionDatum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollisionDatum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTraceLaw","lean:module:QOU.Brings.BringUTContactChirality"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.canonical_residue_not_self_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.canonical_residue_not_self_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L374-L378","doc":"**The canonical residue is not its own mirror either** (geodesic ruling, `ℓ = −1/6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bring_residue_not_self_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bring_residue_not_self_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L368-L372","doc":"**The Bring residue is not its own mirror in `ℚ/ℤ`**: no integer shift takes `1/6` to `−1/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.chiral_of_residue_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.chiral_of_residue_odd","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L362-L366","doc":"**A residue-sensitive energy is chiral**: Part D's achirality hypothesis fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.mirror_symmetric_iff_residue_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.mirror_symmetric_iff_residue_even","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L354-L360","doc":"**Reflection symmetry at a residue is residue-evenness**, for a covariant energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.θstar_eq_pi_div_two_of_achiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.θstar_eq_pi_div_two_of_achiral","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L316-L321","doc":"**If the Bring term is achiral, the selected angle is perpendicular** — so a chiral\nselection (`σ` over `σ⁻¹`) is possible only if the Bring term breaks `θ ↦ π − θ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.unique","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L313-L313","doc":"And the only one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.isMin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.isMin","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L311-L311","doc":"It is a minimiser of the total local energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.θstar_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.θstar_mem","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L309-L309","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.θstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.θstar","kind":"def","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L308-L308","doc":"The selected incoming angle, which starts the Reeb (geodesic) flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.bring","kind":"def","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L306-L306","doc":"The Bring-surface part of the local energy, as a function of the angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L304-L304","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.SegmentCollisionDatum","kind":"class","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L300-L314","doc":"**The segment collision datum** at closest distance `d` and segment half-length `ℓ`:\na Bring contribution to the local energy, and the selected angle, which is the unique\nminimiser on `(0, π)` of O'Hara + Bring. No instance is supplied: the Bring term\nhas no derivation yet (bean `qou-pzsi`, route 2 undefined). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.minimiser_eq_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.minimiser_eq_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L283-L290","doc":"**A reflection-symmetric energy with a unique minimiser on `(0, π)` selects the\nperpendicular crossing.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy_neg_d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy_neg_d","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L279-L281","doc":"**The local O'Hara term is blind to over/under**: `E(−d) = E(d)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel_neg_d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel_neg_d","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L275-L277","doc":"Swapping which segment passes over (`d ↦ −d`) leaves the kernel unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L267-L273","doc":"**The local O'Hara term is chirality-blind**: `E(π − θ) = E(θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L261-L265","doc":"Reversing one segment is the reflection `t ↦ −t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segEnergy","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L257-L259","doc":"The local cross-term energy of two segments of half-length `ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.segKernel","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L253-L255","doc":"The O'Hara/Möbius cross-term kernel of two straight segments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.alt_weight_ne_zero_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.alt_weight_ne_zero_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L239-L243","doc":"**Both channels are live under convention D** (`t ≠ 0`): the Alt weight\n`t q²/(q²+1)²` does not vanish, so the two-box bridge is not annihilated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.channel_weights_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.channel_weights_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L228-L237","doc":"**Convention D channel weights.** At `z = q³/(q²+1)` the Sym and Alt weights are\n`t (q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)²` and `t q²/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.channel_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.channel_weights","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L213-L226","doc":"**Channel weights from a state on `span {1, g}`.** With `g = q·P_S − q⁻¹·P_A`,\n`P_S + P_A = 1`, a state of total `t` and `g`-value `z t` has these weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.chain3_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.chain3_trace","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L184-L203","doc":"**Three solved pieces, two single-crossing bonds**: the composite trace is the product\nof the pieces' traces and the two bonds' Markov values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bondLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bondLetter","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L181-L182","doc":"A single-crossing bond letter at generator `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.window_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.window_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L152-L164","doc":"**Same top block ⇒ same window state.** Stated without division:\n`tr(a x)·tr(a') = tr(a' x)·tr(a)` for `a = L N`, `a' = L' N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.window_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.window_factor","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L145-L150","doc":"**Window factorisation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**Two particles with the same trace are indistinguishable to a single-segment\ncollision**, whatever their histories. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_local_state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_local_state","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L110-L125","doc":"**Universality of the single-segment marginal.** For every letter\n`c = α + β g + γ g⁻¹` on the bridge, the collision functional is the universal\nMarkov value of `c` times `tr a * tr b`. Neither particle's history enters except\nthrough its trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_crossing_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_crossing_inv","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**The inverse bridge crossing sees only `z⁻` times the free product.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**The bridge crossing sees only `z` times the free product.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SegmentCollision.bridge_free","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SegmentCollisionDatum.lean#L85-L90","doc":"**The bridge sees the free product.** Particle `a` below the bridge, particle `b`\nabove it: their unbridged composite has trace `tr a * tr b`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}